  "limitations": [
    "Explicit text bindings are not semantic proof.",
    "Local regression counts must not be pooled with adversarial episodes or interpreted as production security.",
    "Network and supply modules are adapter contracts; deployment enforcement is not established.",
    "The incident map is an architectural reading of a public disclosure, not a reconstruction, and claims no prevention.",
    "The frontier-control tests are deterministic local scenarios; they do not reproduce frontier-model propensities.",
    "Host isolation is measured from inside a cooperative process; it establishes the absence of a path from this process, not the absence of every path, and is no substitute for an adversarial exercise in the target deployment.",
    "Transport is qualified against a controlled loopback peer; the evidence is marked as such and the promotion gate refuses it as production evidence.",
    "Tool-supply controls enforce identity, definition and naming; the behaviour of a remote server when called is not attested.",
    "Monitor rates measured offline describe scripted monitors and are not detector accuracy; an attacker operating inside its granted envelope evades a metadata-only monitor by construction.",
    "The institutional utility and fairness study is not run; the instrument refuses conclusions from synthetic fixtures.",
    "The residual-channel measurement is an upper bound from distinct observable traces under one encoder; it is not a proof that no encoder conveys more, and it bounds only the mediated release interface.",
    "Closing the residual channel costs availability: most adversarial tasks escalate to a named human, and the sealed policy pays for cover traffic, maximum padding and a coarse release schedule."
  ],
  "regression_source_sha256": "92b058fe53c902902329385e9a2f27930a434a23228f53c66adb45bcf5fe2518"
